Z||000009||turbo86se||01-18-2000||01:18 AM||||I second HF6582, I ordered a strut-lid <BR>kit for my 88 coupe after being whacked <BR>on the head too many times when I added <BR>the factory spoiler. Rodney is very easy <BR>to deal with, fast shipping, and a <BR>valuable member in the Fiero community. His products are very high in quality, and I would recommend him to any Fiero owner anywhere!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000010||Carrolles||01-18-2000||08:37 AM||||I met Rodney at the swap meet at Ed Park's place last year.  He is very easy to deal with and his items are of good quality.  I ordered the intake sticker, ball joint tool, and dew strip tool.  They arrived in short time and look great.||||reg||1
Z||000011||mrfixit58||01-18-2000||08:53 AM||||I ordered a tach filter from him and while I was on the phone with him, I asked him about his ball jount removal tool. I told him I was about to do a disc brake conversion on my 68 CAMARO and wondered if his tool would work. He told me to measure the distance between the ball joints and when I did he said the Fiero tool was too short. But, he offered to make one long enough to work AND he threw in the part necessary to make it work on a Fiero as well... FOR NO ADDITIONAL COST!!! Great guy! Got the parts in a few days and they were great!||||reg||14
Z||000012||fiero56||01-18-2000||10:36 AM||||I met Rodney at the '99 nationals in Colubus. He is a great guy. Between a buddy and me, we bought 3rd brake light steel plate, a couple key chains, some steel Ferrari "plates", and sever other items I don't recall right now. Everything he had there was high quality, and he was very friendly and helpfull. No wonder his booth was one of the most crowded there.||||reg||10
